/*****************************************************************************
    T1 -- SAME ACTION, RECURSING. SEQ 31's decisive test.

    emitPlan's shape exactly, and it decides whether iterators reach genParse:
    every interesting walk there is recursive.

    Self-terminating by construction -- a, b and c carry no list, so the inner
    walk's iterate hits the no-list guard and the loop never runs.

    NOTE THE SHAPE: the loop body is a SINGLE statement and the print happens at
    ENTRY. That is not style -- aCTionCodE's box scan finds the first `{` and
    then scans to the FIRST `}` with NO NESTING COUNT, so a `{ }` block inside a
    code={} body truncates the box at the inner brace. Nested blocks are not
    available here.

    PER-FRAME  -> at triple, at a, at b, at c   (4 lines, terminates)
                  Each frame gets its own cursor. Iterators reach emitPlan.
    SHARED     -> anything else. The inner iterate disturbs the outer cursor, so
                  the walk is short, repeating, or spins. Iterators do NOT reach
                  genParse and minion A's step 3 goes back to hand-rolled walks.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(IterTest);
define
    triple  a b c;

    walk argument code={
        print "at " taG argument:;
        iterate grup on argument;
        while ++grup
            walk(grup);
        };
    ;

walk(triple);
stop();
